{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CLOSING EVIDENCE — all 7 children closed, all 5 epic ACs live-proven on Bedrock.\n\nAC1 (runaway detected DURING run, aborted, routed to verdict): c827 merged (Gerrit 1447, 125163c94d) + fd84. Four consecutive production captures during this session's own closes: aborts at 84, 158, 83, and 67 requests (vs the historical 240-request burnouts), each followed by bounded recovery delivering a real verdict. Two captures had max_consecutive_repeat=1 — rotating k-cycles the old adjacent metric was provably blind to (70bc); the windowed distinct-ratio (window 24, trip <=0.50) fired on all.\n\nAC2 (no mid-run tool-surface emptying / Bedrock toolConfig 400): e1b1 closed; the c827 guard raises BEFORE executing the repeated call and never empties the surface; zero Bedrock 400s across all live runs (exp_i/k/l + four gate closes).\n\nAC3 (every exhaustion/runaway leaves gate_error_v1 with repetition counters): 8b97 (render at raise_completion_workflow_failure) + 215f (diagnostic survives prelude failure; Gerrit 1448 merged 4792fac4b9). Live: the c827 close-failure sidecar carried full counters and drove the ed6d bug report directly from its diagnostic.\n\nAC4 (durable usage recording incl. loop-vs-breadth axis): aec1 closed — tool_calls + distinct + max_consecutive_repeat + distinct_ratio_window recorded by default; every WARNING line quoted above came from that instrumentation.\n\nAC5 (healthy breadth never truncated): test_healthy_run_past_flat_landing_threshold_is_never_aborted (Gerrit 1450 merged 9a27202837) — a 251-request high-novelty run lands naturally past the old 239 flat-landing threshold; the 94a3 and 215f closes also completed through the gate without truncation.\n\nEnd-to-end validation: 94a3-1323-3497-4f59 (the parallel session's stuck ticket, four prior exhaustions) closed + signed through the new gate without --force. Residual defect discovered while dogfooding filed as ed6d-5448-4ff6-4b8a (P1, discovered_from c827): one criterion's evidence-run exhaustion kills whole bounded recovery — plan written and signed, not a blocker for this epic's ACs."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785985843492954001,"uuid":"00a041cd-91c1-4f9d-8f9a-e4ced8ea8f44"}